# Wolseley 14/60 four-door saloon, 1938-1948.
#
# The 1,818 cc six of the 1938 Wolseley range; the 14/60 uses the narrower
# 12/48 shell and shares the 2.654 m wheelbase with the 16/65 and 18/85.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolseley_14/60
#
# Dimensions: overall figures were not established. The model measures 4.26 x
# 1.56 x 1.65 m on the 2.654 m family wheelbase, ESTIMATED from the
# photographs; these are not specifications. The narrower 12/48 shell is used,
# not the 18/85 width.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side profile exists. Image 1 is about 25
# degrees off side; the flank is estimated from it and the front view within
# the published wheelbase. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period chart was found. Black, grey, green and
# maroon are plain names. Weights 12, 10, 10, 8, total 40, provisional.
#
# Speed 120 km/h. Comfort 55/413, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 55. Classes 1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 1938 intro, retires staggered 1958-1961.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/wolseley-14-60.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/wolseley-14-60.dae. References:
# citycars/references/wolseley-14-60/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: there is no true side or rear view, so the flank and
# overall dimensions are estimated and the tail inferred. The front wing sweep
# and bonnet-side trim are simplified. At 128 px the narrow six-light body and
# Wolseley grille read as a 14/60.


obj=citycar
